 "notes": "Plan of the SS Thistlegorm (126.5 x 17.7 m) lying upright on sand at 30-32 m, bow about 16 m, hull drawn bow NNW/NW (330 degrees; guides describe a roughly north-south wreck, the exact heading is an assumption). Layout of holds, blast area, locomotives and stern guns from dive-guide descriptions (dive-the-world.com, aquariusredsea.com, divers-guide.com) and first-hand observation; positions are approximate. Boats tie their own lines to the wreck (the HEPCA moorings were lost), so no fixed mooring is drawn; the route: holds 3-2-1, the port locomotive, the stern, propeller and guns.",
